INSERT INTO guides (file, title, category, blurb, related, media_id, sort) VALUES ('dog-treat-recipes.jpg','5 Homemade Dog Treat Recipes','Dogs','Bone broth pupsicles, meal mixer training cookies, no-bake bites, frozen enrichment Kongs and birthday pupcakes — plus the ingredients that are toxic to dogs.','/blog/stella-and-chewys-dog-food-review', 96, 8);
INSERT INTO posts (slug, title, description, keywords, category, hero_image, body_html, status, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('stella-and-chewys-dog-food-review','Stella &amp; Chewys Review 2026: Top 10 Foods + 5 Treat Recipes','An honest Stella and Chewys review — the rescue-dog founding story, how freeze-dried raw actually works, our top 10 picks across dry, freeze-dried and wet, the real drawbacks, and 5 homemade treat recipes.','Stella and Chewys review, Stella and Chewys dog food, freeze dried raw dog food, best raw dog food, raw coated kibble, Stella and Chewys meal mixers, bone broth for dogs, homemade dog treat recipes, is raw dog food safe, dog food review 2026','Dogs', '','<p>In 1997, a woman in Brooklyn walked into an animal shelter and was told not to adopt one of the dogs. He was too sick, the vet said — an autoimmune disease, a poor prognosis, not a sensible choice. She adopted him anyway. His name was Chewy.</p>
<p>That decision is why this brand exists. Marie Moody''s vet suggested trying a raw diet of protein, fruit and vegetables, so she started making Chewy''s meals herself in her brownstone kitchen. His health turned around dramatically. By <strong>2003 she had turned it into a company</strong>, named for Chewy and her other rescue dog, Stella — and today Stella &amp; Chewy''s runs a 355,000 square foot facility in Oak Creek, Wisconsin, a long way from that first kitchen.</p>
<p>It''s a genuinely lovely origin story. But a lovely story isn''t a reason to spend $40 on a bag of dog food, so this review covers what actually matters: what makes their food different, our top 10 picks across freeze-dried raw, dry kibble and wet food, the real benefits, the honest drawbacks — including the raw-food safety question most brand reviews skip — and five fun recipes you can make at home using their products.</p>

<div class="quick-facts">
  <h3>🐕 Stella &amp; Chewy''s at a Glance</h3>
  <div class="qf-grid">
    <div class="qf-item"><span class="qf-label">Founded</span><span class="qf-value">2003, by Marie Moody</span></div>
    <div class="qf-item"><span class="qf-label">Named after</span><span class="qf-value">Her two rescue dogs, adopted 1997</span></div>
    <div class="qf-item"><span class="qf-label">Based in</span><span class="qf-value">Oak Creek, Wisconsin, USA</span></div>
    <div class="qf-item"><span class="qf-label">Known for</span><span class="qf-value">Freeze-dried raw — the category leader</span></div>
    <div class="qf-item"><span class="qf-label">Safety process</span><span class="qf-value">HPP since 2007 + every batch tested</span></div>
    <div class="qf-item"><span class="qf-label">Certification</span><span class="qf-value">SQF Level 2, APHIS for export</span></div>
    <div class="qf-item"><span class="qf-label">Typical meat content</span><span class="qf-value">95% meat, organ &amp; bone (freeze-dried)</span></div>
    <div class="qf-item"><span class="qf-label">Price bracket</span><span class="qf-value">Premium — $20–$97 depending on line</span></div>
  </div>
</div>

<h2>📖 The Story Behind the Name</h2>
<p>Marie Moody adopted Stella and Chewy in 1997. Chewy was the one the shelter''s vet advised against — he was diagnosed with an autoimmune disease and simply wasn''t thriving. When conventional feeding wasn''t working, the vet suggested a raw diet built around protein, fruits and vegetables, and Marie began preparing it by hand.</p>
<p>Chewy''s recovery was the thing that convinced her. She started making the food commercially in <strong>2003</strong>, working out of her Brooklyn brownstone kitchen before moving production to Wisconsin — first a 10,000 square foot plant in Muskego, and eventually the 355,000 square foot facility in Oak Creek the company operates today. The tagline that came out of all this, <em>"only the good stuff,"</em> is still on every bag.</p>
<div class="funfact">
  <span class="ff-label">🎉 Worth knowing</span>
  <p>The brand is named after two <strong>rescue dogs</strong>, and one of them was a dog a professional recommended against adopting. Whatever you conclude about the food, that''s a genuinely nice piece of pet industry history — and it''s why the packaging carries two dogs'' faces rather than a stock photo.</p>
</div>

<h2>🔬 What Actually Makes It Different</h2>
<p>Plenty of brands claim to be premium. Here''s what''s specifically different about this one, and what each point means in practice.</p>

<h3>1. They pasteurise raw food with pressure, not heat</h3>
<p>The central objection to raw pet food is pathogens. Stella &amp; Chewy''s adopted <strong>high-pressure processing (HPP) in 2007</strong>, ahead of most of the industry. HPP subjects sealed food to enormous water pressure, which destroys pathogens like <em>Salmonella</em> and <em>Listeria</em> <strong>without cooking it</strong> — so the nutritional profile of raw is preserved while the microbial risk drops dramatically. They also state that every batch is tested before release, and hold SQF Level 2 certification.</p>
<p>This matters more than any marketing claim on the front of the bag. It''s the single biggest reason we''re comfortable recommending their raw products when we''d be more cautious about frozen raw generally.</p>

<h3>2. Freeze-drying, not cooking</h3>
<p>Freeze-drying removes water at low temperature under vacuum, leaving the protein structure, fats and heat-sensitive nutrients largely intact. The result is shelf-stable food you store in a cupboard rather than a freezer, that rehydrates with warm water in about a minute, and that doesn''t need the high-heat extrusion that conventional kibble goes through.</p>

<h3>3. Very high meat inclusion</h3>
<p>Their freeze-dried raw recipes are typically <strong>95% meat, organs and bone</strong> — with the organ and bone content being the important part. Muscle meat alone is not a complete diet for a dog; organs supply vitamin A, iron, copper and B vitamins, and ground bone supplies calcium and phosphorus in roughly the ratio a dog evolved to use.</p>

<h3>4. They offer grain-free <em>and</em> grain-inclusive</h3>
<p>Their Wild Red kibble comes in both a grain and legume-free version and a <strong>Wholesome Grains</strong> version, and the SuperBlends line is built around digestible grains, superfoods, bone broth and probiotics. Given the ongoing conversation about grain-free diets (more on that below), having both options available is a genuinely sensible position rather than a marketing hedge.</p>

<h3>5. Probiotics in everything</h3>
<p>Live probiotics and antioxidants are added across the range. Dogs on antibiotics, dogs recovering from digestive upsets and dogs transitioning between foods all benefit from supported gut flora — and gut health is where a lot of the "my dog''s coat got shinier" feedback ultimately comes from.</p>

<h2>🧩 The Formats Explained (This Confuses Everyone)</h2>
<p>Their biggest weakness is arguably how many product lines they have. Here''s what each one actually is.</p>
<div class="table-wrap">
  <table class="compare">
    <thead><tr><th>Format</th><th>What it is</th><th>Use it as</th><th>Best for</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>Freeze-Dried Dinner Patties</b></td><td>95% meat/organ/bone, freeze-dried into patties. Rehydrate with warm water</td><td>A complete meal</td><td>Full raw feeding without a freezer</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Meal Mixers</b></td><td>The same raw, in smaller morsels</td><td>Topper or complete meal</td><td>Boosting an existing kibble</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Marie''s Magical Dinner Dust</b></td><td>Powdered freeze-dried raw</td><td>Sprinkle topper</td><td>Picky eaters — the cheapest way in</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Stella''s Solutions</b></td><td>Freeze-dried raw plus targeted functional ingredients</td><td>Topper</td><td>Digestive, hip &amp; joint, immune, skin &amp; coat, heart</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Raw Coated Kibble</b></td><td>Kibble with a freeze-dried raw coating on every piece</td><td>A complete meal</td><td>Kibble convenience, raw boost</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Raw Blend Kibble</b></td><td>Raw-coated kibble <em>plus</em> loose freeze-dried raw pieces mixed in</td><td>A complete meal</td><td>The best dry-food option they make</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Stella''s Shredrs</b></td><td>Shredded meat in broth, in pouches</td><td>Complete meal or topper</td><td>Hydration, seniors, fussy dogs</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Bountiful Bone Broth</b></td><td>Bone broth with turmeric and joint support</td><td>Topper / hydration</td><td>Seniors, dogs off their food, recovery</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
<div class="vet-tip">
  <h4>💚 The simplest way to decide</h4>
  <p>If you want <strong>raw without a freezer</strong> → Dinner Patties. If you want to <strong>upgrade the kibble you already buy</strong> → Meal Mixers or Dinner Dust. If you want <strong>one bag that does everything</strong> → Raw Blend Kibble. If your dog is <strong>fussy, elderly or needs more water</strong> → Shredrs or Bone Broth.</p>
</div>
<h2>🏆 Our Top 10 Stella &amp; Chewy''s Products</h2>
<p>Ranked across all three formats — freeze-dried raw, dry kibble and wet food — with who each one is actually for.</p>

<div class="product">
  <div class="product-ribbon"><span class="rank"><span class="star">★</span> #1 · Best Overall</span><span class="asin">Freeze-Dried Raw</span></div>
  <div class="product-body">
    <div class="product-image-wrap"><div class="product-image-placeholder">📷 Product photo coming soon</div></div>
    <div class="product-content">
      <div class="product-title">Stella''s Super Beef Freeze-Dried Raw Dinner Patties</div>
      <div class="product-price"><span class="dollar">$39.99</span><span class="disclaimer">*14 oz · price starts from and is subject to change</span></div>
      <span class="best-for">Best For: Full raw feeding · Grass-fed beef · No freezer needed</span>
      <div class="product-desc">
        <p>The flagship, and the product that built the brand. 95% grass-fed beef, organs and bone, freeze-dried into patties you crumble and rehydrate with warm water. Complete and balanced to AAFCO standards, with added probiotics and taurine.</p>
        <p>This is raw feeding with the two biggest obstacles removed — no freezer space and no thawing schedule. Comes in 5.5 oz and 14 oz bags, so you can trial it before committing.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pros-cons">
        <div class="pros"><h4>Pros</h4><ul><li>95% meat, organ and bone</li><li>Complete meal, not just a topper</li><li>Shelf-stable — cupboard, not freezer</li><li>HPP treated and batch tested</li></ul></div>
        <div class="cons"><h4>Cons</h4><ul><li>Expensive as a sole diet for a big dog</li><li>Needs rehydrating properly</li><li>Grain-free — see our note below</li></ul></div>
      </div>
      <a class="cta-btn" href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Stella+and+Chewys+Super+Beef+freeze+dried+dinner+patties" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener sponsored">Check price on Amazon</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="product">
  <div class="product-ribbon"><span class="rank"><span class="star">★</span> #2 · Best Dry Food</span><span class="asin">Raw Blend Kibble</span></div>
  <div class="product-body">
    <div class="product-image-wrap"><div class="product-image-placeholder">📷 Product photo coming soon</div></div>
    <div class="product-content">
      <div class="product-title">Wild Red Raw Blend Kibble — Red Meat Recipe</div>
      <div class="product-price"><span class="dollar">$96.99</span><span class="disclaimer">*21 lb · price starts from and is subject to change</span></div>
      <span class="best-for">Best For: One-bag convenience · High animal protein · Multi-protein variety</span>
      <div class="product-desc">
        <p>If you want the benefits of raw without changing how you feed, this is the pick. Every kibble piece is coated in freeze-dried raw <em>and</em> there are loose freeze-dried raw pieces mixed through the bag — the difference between "Raw Blend" and the cheaper "Raw Coated" line.</p>
        <p>Six meat proteins (beef, pork, lamb, bison, venison, goat) and around 89–90% animal protein in the grain-free version. Also available as Prairie (six poultry proteins) and Ocean (six fish proteins), and in a Wholesome Grains version.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pros-cons">
        <div class="pros"><h4>Pros</h4><ul><li>Raw benefits with kibble convenience</li><li>Very high animal protein percentage</li><li>Grain-free or wholesome grains option</li><li>Probiotics included</li></ul></div>
        <div class="cons"><h4>Cons</h4><ul><li>Premium price per bag</li><li>Frequently out of stock</li><li>Rich — transition slowly</li></ul></div>
      </div>
      <a class="cta-btn cta-green" href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Stella+and+Chewys+Wild+Red+Raw+Blend+dry+dog+food" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener sponsored">Check price on Amazon</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="product">
  <div class="product-ribbon"><span class="rank"><span class="star">★</span> #3 · Best Wet Food</span><span class="asin">Wet · Shreds in Broth</span></div>
  <div class="product-body">
    <div class="product-image-wrap"><div class="product-image-placeholder">📷 Product photo coming soon</div></div>
    <div class="product-content">
      <div class="product-title">Stella''s Shredrs Cage-Free Chicken Recipe in Broth</div>
      <div class="product-price"><span class="dollar">$31.08</span><span class="disclaimer">*multipack of 2.8 oz pouches · subject to change</span></div>
      <span class="best-for">Best For: Hydration · Senior dogs · Fussy eaters · Post-illness recovery</span>
      <div class="product-desc">
        <p>Real shredded meat in broth rather than a uniform pâté, which matters because texture is often what wins over a dog that''s gone off its food. Grain-free, limited ingredient, and works either as a complete meal or spooned over kibble.</p>
        <p>The broth content is the underrated part — it''s an easy way to get more water into a dog that doesn''t drink enough, which supports kidney and urinary health across a long life. Available in eight protein combinations including beef, duck, turkey, salmon and lamb.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pros-cons">
        <div class="pros"><h4>Pros</h4><ul><li>Excellent moisture content</li><li>Real shredded texture tempts fussy dogs</li><li>Complete meal or topper</li><li>Several proteins for rotation</li></ul></div>
        <div class="cons"><h4>Cons</h4><ul><li>Small pouches — costly for large dogs</li><li>More packaging waste</li></ul></div>
      </div>
      <a class="cta-btn cta-teal" href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Stella+and+Chewys+Shredrs+wet+dog+food+broth" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener sponsored">Check price on Amazon</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="product">
  <div class="product-ribbon"><span class="rank"><span class="star">★</span> #4 · Best Way to Start</span><span class="asin">Freeze-Dried · Topper</span></div>
  <div class="product-body">
    <div class="product-image-wrap"><div class="product-image-placeholder">📷 Product photo coming soon</div></div>
    <div class="product-content">
      <div class="product-title">Meal Mixers — Stella''s Super Beef</div>
      <div class="product-price"><span class="dollar">$22.99</span><span class="disclaimer">*sizes from 1 oz to 35 oz · subject to change</span></div>
      <span class="best-for">Best For: Trying raw without committing · Boosting existing kibble</span>
      <div class="product-desc">
        <p>The same 95% meat, organ and bone as the dinner patties, in smaller morsels designed to scatter over whatever you already feed. This is where we''d tell most people to start: you get the palatability and nutritional lift of raw at a fraction of the cost of switching entirely.</p>
        <p>The 1 oz sample size is genuinely useful — it costs very little to find out whether your dog is interested before buying a full bag.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pros-cons">
        <div class="pros"><h4>Pros</h4><ul><li>Cheapest way to trial the brand</li><li>Transforms a boring kibble bowl</li><li>Can be fed as a complete meal too</li><li>Tiny trial sizes available</li></ul></div>
        <div class="cons"><h4>Cons</h4><ul><li>Adds calories — reduce kibble accordingly</li><li>Large bags are pricey</li></ul></div>
      </div>
      <a class="cta-btn" href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Stella+and+Chewys+Meal+Mixers+freeze+dried+raw" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener sponsored">Check price on Amazon</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="product">
  <div class="product-ribbon"><span class="rank"><span class="star">★</span> #5 · Best With Grains</span><span class="asin">Dry · SuperBlends</span></div>
  <div class="product-body">
    <div class="product-image-wrap"><div class="product-image-placeholder">📷 Product photo coming soon</div></div>
    <div class="product-content">
      <div class="product-title">SuperBlends Raw Coated Kibble — Beef, Beef Liver &amp; Lamb + Superfoods</div>
      <div class="product-price"><span class="dollar">$82.99</span><span class="disclaimer">*subject to change · Raw Blend version $96.99</span></div>
      <span class="best-for">Best For: Owners who''d rather avoid grain-free · Digestive support</span>
      <div class="product-desc">
        <p>Built around highly digestible wholesome grains, superfoods, bone broth and probiotics rather than the legume-heavy formulations that dominate grain-free food. For anyone who has read about the grain-free and heart disease investigation and would prefer to sidestep the question entirely, this is the line to look at.</p>
        <p>Also available in Chicken &amp; Duck, Whitefish &amp; Salmon, and a puppy formula.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pros-cons">
        <div class="pros"><h4>Pros</h4><ul><li>Grain-inclusive — avoids the DCM debate</li><li>Bone broth and superfoods included</li><li>Raw Coated or Raw Blend versions</li><li>Puppy formula available</li></ul></div>
        <div class="cons"><h4>Cons</h4><ul><li>Lower animal protein % than Wild Red</li><li>Premium price</li></ul></div>
      </div>
      <a class="cta-btn cta-green" href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Stella+and+Chewys+SuperBlends+dry+dog+food" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener sponsored">Check price on Amazon</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="callout">
  <div class="callout-body">
    A dog eating a moisture-rich, highly digestible diet drinks differently, digests differently and passes noticeably smaller, firmer stools. That last one isn''t a cosmetic detail — it''s the clearest everyday signal you have that more of the food is actually being absorbed rather than passing straight through.
    <span class="callout-attr">— The Pet-GoToPro Editorial Team</span>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="product">
  <div class="product-ribbon"><span class="rank"><span class="star">★</span> #6 · Best First Protein</span><span class="asin">Freeze-Dried Raw</span></div>
  <div class="product-body">
    <div class="product-image-wrap"><div class="product-image-placeholder">📷 Product photo coming soon</div></div>
    <div class="product-content">
      <div class="product-title">Chewy''s Chicken Freeze-Dried Raw Dinner Patties</div>
      <div class="product-price"><span class="dollar">$35.99</span><span class="disclaimer">*14 oz · subject to change</span></div>
      <span class="best-for">Best For: First-time raw · Milder protein · Named after the founding dog</span>
      <div class="product-desc">
        <p>95% cage-free chicken, organs and bone. Chicken is generally the gentlest starting protein for a dog moving to raw for the first time, and it''s usually the cheapest in the range — a sensible combination for a trial run.</p>
        <p>It''s also, pleasingly, named after the rescue dog whose recovery started the whole company.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pros-cons">
        <div class="pros"><h4>Pros</h4><ul><li>Mild, widely tolerated protein</li><li>One of the lower prices in the line</li><li>Complete and balanced</li></ul></div>
        <div class="cons"><h4>Cons</h4><ul><li>Chicken is a common allergen for some dogs</li><li>Not a novel protein</li></ul></div>
      </div>
      <a class="cta-btn" href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Stella+and+Chewys+Chewys+Chicken+freeze+dried+dinner+patties" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener sponsored">Check price on Amazon</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="product">
  <div class="product-ribbon"><span class="rank"><span class="star">★</span> #7 · Best for Puppies</span><span class="asin">Freeze-Dried Raw</span></div>
  <div class="product-body">
    <div class="product-image-wrap"><div class="product-image-placeholder">📷 Product photo coming soon</div></div>
    <div class="product-content">
      <div class="product-title">Perfectly Puppy Beef &amp; Salmon Dinner Patties</div>
      <div class="product-price"><span class="dollar">$35.99</span><span class="disclaimer">*subject to change · Meal Mixer version $43.99</span></div>
      <span class="best-for">Best For: Puppies · Brain and eye development · Growth</span>
      <div class="product-desc">
        <p>95% beef, salmon, organs and bone, formulated for growth rather than adult maintenance — which matters, because puppies have genuinely different calcium, phosphorus and calorie requirements and shouldn''t simply eat smaller portions of adult food.</p>
        <p>The salmon supplies <strong>DHA</strong>, an omega-3 fatty acid with a well-established role in brain and eye development during the first year.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pros-cons">
        <div class="pros"><h4>Pros</h4><ul><li>Formulated for growth, not adults</li><li>DHA for brain and eye development</li><li>Available as patties or mixers</li></ul></div>
        <div class="cons"><h4>Cons</h4><ul><li>Large-breed puppies need careful calcium management — ask your vet</li><li>Expensive during the hungriest life stage</li></ul></div>
      </div>
      <a class="cta-btn cta-purple" href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Stella+and+Chewys+Perfectly+Puppy+freeze+dried+raw" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener sponsored">Check price on Amazon</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="product">
  <div class="product-ribbon"><span class="rank"><span class="star">★</span> #8 · Best for Picky Eaters</span><span class="asin">Freeze-Dried · Sprinkle</span></div>
  <div class="product-body">
    <div class="product-image-wrap"><div class="product-image-placeholder">📷 Product photo coming soon</div></div>
    <div class="product-content">
      <div class="product-title">Marie''s Magical Dinner Dust</div>
      <div class="product-price"><span class="dollar">$22.99</span><span class="disclaimer">*Bac''n version $27.99 · subject to change</span></div>
      <span class="best-for">Best For: Dogs who won''t eat · Medication disguise · Cheapest entry point</span>
      <div class="product-desc">
        <p>Freeze-dried raw ground into a powder you sprinkle over food. It''s the same 95% meat, organ and bone as everything else in the range, just in the format most likely to convince a dog that today''s dinner is worth eating.</p>
        <p>Available in grass-fed beef, cage-free chicken, Duck Duck Goose and a bacon-and-red-meat version, plus Breakfast Sprinkles in Bacon, Egg &amp; Cheese. Genuinely useful for hiding medication or tempting a dog recovering from illness.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pros-cons">
        <div class="pros"><h4>Pros</h4><ul><li>Extremely effective on fussy dogs</li><li>Small amount goes a long way</li><li>Great for disguising medication</li></ul></div>
        <div class="cons"><h4>Cons</h4><ul><li>A topper, not a meal</li><li>Easy to over-sprinkle — watch calories</li></ul></div>
      </div>
      <a class="cta-btn cta-clay" href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Stella+and+Chewys+Maries+Magical+Dinner+Dust" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener sponsored">Check price on Amazon</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="product">
  <div class="product-ribbon"><span class="rank"><span class="star">★</span> #9 · Best Targeted Support</span><span class="asin">Stella''s Solutions</span></div>
  <div class="product-body">
    <div class="product-image-wrap"><div class="product-image-placeholder">📷 Product photo coming soon</div></div>
    <div class="product-content">
      <div class="product-title">Stella''s Solutions Functional Toppers</div>
      <div class="product-price"><span class="dollar">$31.99</span><span class="disclaimer">*subject to change</span></div>
      <span class="best-for">Best For: Seniors · Itchy skin · Stiff joints · Digestive issues</span>
      <div class="product-desc">
        <p>Freeze-dried raw with targeted functional ingredients added, in five versions: <strong>Digestive Support</strong> (pumpkin, papaya, pineapple), <strong>Hip &amp; Joint</strong> (chicken cartilage, green-lipped mussel, turmeric, omega-3s), <strong>Immune Support</strong> (beta-carotene, berries, omega-3s), <strong>Skin &amp; Coat</strong> (vitamin E, biotin, pineapple) and <strong>Healthy Heart</strong> (chicken hearts, sardines, taurine, DHA).</p>
        <p>The green-lipped mussel in the joint version and the taurine in the heart version are ingredients with genuine evidence behind them — this isn''t purely marketing. That said, a functional topper supports; it does not treat. A limping dog needs a vet, not a supplement.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pros-cons">
        <div class="pros"><h4>Pros</h4><ul><li>Real functional ingredients, not just flavour</li><li>Five targeted options</li><li>Raw nutrition at the same time</li></ul></div>
